        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>AZ&#39;s Fueled Freeze is a good card to save until he&#39;s flipped -- you can clear out all three and hit Plague Rat for pretty solid damage, especially if you&#39;ve got any buffs (Twist the Ether and Focused Apertures).</p><p>AZ is going to be doing a lot of the legwork here. Get the Null Point Calibration unit out as soon as possible, followed by Twist the Ether and Infection -- you&#39;re now automatically healing AZ for 3 each turn, 4 if you get Focused Apertures out. It also makes all the cards that should do AZ fire damage into massive heals -- Hoarfire, Frost-Bound Drain and Thermal Shockwave will let him heal 10s of HP in a round with this set-up.</p><p>Get Twist the Ether on Plague Rat next and keep AZ&#39;s HP high, and he should outright absorb most of the Rat&#39;s big attacks. Use Visionary&#39;s power to get AZ his cards quicker, he&#39;s the top priority. As mentioned, use her to deal with the environment, either mind controlling a Kraken or using her cards to influence the deck.</p><p>Tempest should get Cleansing Downpour on the table as soon as possible and use it as his primary power. Into The Stratosphere is a good way to stall Plague Rat if you toss an Infection card (It&#39;s not destroying it, so it doesn&#39;t incur that attack) or Plague Locus on top of his deck.</p><p>If you can keep ahead of Plague Rat&#39;s constant damage, it&#39;s doable. Tough, but doable.</p><p>Edit: Well, a day late and a dollar short, I guess.</p>",
